        "raw": "<p>It took four tries, but managed it.&nbsp; Took a team of Ra, Tempest, Nightmist, and Argent Adept.&nbsp; The environement was Pike Industrial Complex.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Tempest and Ra did a good job in the early game scrubbing out the thugs and underbosses.&nbsp; Nightmist got her amulet out one round too late to stop the Hired Gun, though, and that hurt (7 damage each).</p><p>By the time the five underbosses were down, everyone was down to single digit hit points, and it looked like a lost game.&nbsp; When neither of the main damage dealers can survive doing their damage, it starts to look bleak.</p><p>Then, Nightmist used Mistbound to stop the Chairman from drawing cards, and Argent Adept and Tempest did a good job of keeping it cycled (Reclaim from the Deep and Vernal Sonata).&nbsp; That stopped most of Chairman&#39;s offensive output.&nbsp; Sadly, Tempest never drew his healing card, which would have helped the end game immensely.&nbsp; Ra and Tempest ended up spending too many turns idle, because they couldn&#39;t survive the damage coming back to them.&nbsp; Ra started playing redundant Staff of Ra cards just to get the 3 hp back.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Basically, the end game consisted of Nightmist and AA tying up Chairman and Operative, and arranging turns where either Ra or Tempest could attack with good economy of damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It was a fun game, and it felt one Vat explosion away from defeat.</p>",
